ts1.34/1.35/1.36 variants. This supports modern-version tailoring; it does not identify the actual MPN host version.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/docs/concepts/platform/supported-distributions.mdx",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. Inherited MPN host-control recommendation for: The Kubernetes KubeletConfiguration file must be owned by root. The official check addresses host/control-plane binaries, flags, files, native logging, node services or encryption, not an application behavior. The selected Horizon package deploys namespaced workloads atop Core and does not provision those host settings. Current scope assigns that boundary to MPN; this designation means proposed inherited coverage, not source confirmation of the exact host setting or a formal pass. No application remediation is inferred from absence of the host configuration in the application repo.\n\nNext action: Carry the exact official check into the MPN-owned Kubernetes baseline/checklist and link its inherited result; do not treat the ownership assertion as evidence of an observed native setting."
