          "stig_uuid": "92b6f33f-228f-5363-afb6-9f95dc57a4b5",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: Inherited MPN host-control recommendation for: Kubernetes Controller Manager must disable profiling. The official check addresses host/control-plane binaries, flags, files, native logging, node services or encryption, not an application behavior. The selected Horizon package deploys namespaced workloads atop Core and does not provision those host settings. Current scope assigns that boundary to MPN; this designation means proposed inherited coverage, not source confirmation of the exact host setting or a formal pass. No application remediation is inferred from absence of the host configuration in the application repo.\n\nComponents: MPN cluster and nodes; Gallatin horizon-uds workloads\n\nOwner: Gallatin SRE (UDS Core); MPN node/control-plane owner for host configuration\n\nNext action: Carry the exact official check into the MPN-owned Kubernetes baseline/checklist and link its inherited result; do not treat the ownership assertion as evidence of an observed native setting.\n\nEvidence:\n[host] MPN ownership\nCurrent scope assigns control plane/node OS to MPN; no host assessment or live configuration was supplied.\nhttps://gallatin.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/GG/pages/733085804/WIP+STIG+SRG+Compliance+Scope+MPN\n\n[re-kubernetes-release] re-kubernetes-release\nLatest successful Nov5 UDS push artifact2026.45.4-uds.1 identifies package commit d528b7f, Horizon b84b9af, Core1.14 and identity.mode=uds. Its build-info supplies immutable runtimeSource images; this supersedes the bundled-identity default candidate for this review.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685\n\n[re-kubernetes-supported-versions] re-kubernetes-supported-versions\nPinned Core1.14 documentation covers supported non-EOL CNCF-conformant clusters and tests1.34/1.35/1.36 variants. This supports modern-version tailoring; it does not identify the actual MPN host version.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/docs/concepts/platform/supported-distributions.mdx",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. Inherited MPN host-control recommendation for: Kubernetes Controller Manager must disable profiling. The official check addresses host/control-plane binaries, flags, files, native logging, node services or encryption, not an application behavior. The selected Horizon package deploys namespaced workloads atop Core and does not provision those host settings. Current scope assigns that boundary to MPN; this designation means proposed inherited coverage, not source confirmation of the exact host setting or a formal pass. No application remediation is inferred from absence of the host configuration in the application repo.\n\nNext action: Carry the exact official check into the MPN-owned Kubernetes baseline/checklist and link its inherited result; do not treat the ownership assertion as evidence of an observed native setting."
        },
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-242410",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-242410",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000142-CTR-000325",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-242410",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000142-CTR-000325",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-242410r1043177_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-242410r1043177",
          "rule_version": "CNTR-K8-000920",
          "rule_title": "The Kubernetes API Server must enforce ports, protocols, and services (PPS) that adhere to the Ports, Protocols, and Services Management Category Assurance List (PPSM CAL).",
          "fix_text": "Amend any system documentation requiring revision to comply with PPSM CAL. \n\nUpdate Kubernetes API Server manifest and namespace PPS configuration to comply with PPSM CAL.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Change to the /etc/kubernetes/manifests/ directory on the Kubernetes Control Plane. Run the command:\ngrep kube-apiserver.manifest -I -secure-port *\ngrep kube-apiserver.manifest -I -etcd-servers *\n-edit manifest file:\nVIM <Manifest Name>\nReview livenessProbe:\nHttpGet:\nPort:\nReview ports:\n- containerPort:\nhostPort:\n- containerPort:\nhostPort:\n\nRun command: \nkubectl describe services --all-namespaces \nSearch labels for any apiserver namespaces.\nPort:\n\nAny manifest and namespace PPS or services configuration not in compliance with PPSM CAL is a finding.\n\nReview the information systems documentation and interview the team, gain an understanding of the API Server architecture, and determine applicable PPS. If there are any PPS in the system documentation not in compliance with the CAL PPSM, this is a finding. Any PPS not set in the system documentation is a finding.\n\nReview findings against the most recent PPSM CAL:\nhttps://cyber.mil/ppsm/cal/\n\nVerify API Server network boundary with the PPS associated with the CAL Assurance Categories. Any PPS not in compliance with the CAL Assurance Category requirements is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Kubernetes_STIG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "Kubernetes API Server PPSs must be controlled and conform to the PPSM CAL. Those PPS that fall outside the PPSM CAL must be blocked. Instructions on the PPSM can be found in DoD Instruction 8551.01 Policy.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-000382"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "5376",
          "uuid": "4bbc6216-ded9-5705-8411-33252f0669ef",
          "stig_uuid": "92b6f33f-228f-5363-afb6-9f95dc57a4b5",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
