          "rule_id": "SV-242423r1043178",
          "rule_version": "CNTR-K8-001450",
          "rule_title": "Kubernetes etcd must enable client authentication to secure service.",
          "fix_text": "Edit the Kubernetes etcd manifest file in the /etc/kubernetes/manifests directory on the Kubernetes Control Plane. \n\nSet the value of \"--client-cert-auth\" to \"true\" for the etcd.",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Change to the /etc/kubernetes/manifests directory on the Kubernetes Control Plane. Run the command:\n\ngrep -i client-cert-auth * \n\nIf the setting client-cert-auth is not configured in the Kubernetes etcd manifest file or set to \"false\", this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Kubernetes_STIG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "Kubernetes container and pod configuration are maintained by Kubelet. Kubelet agents register nodes with the API Server, mount volume storage, and perform health checks for containers and pods. Anyone who gains access to Kubelet agents can effectively control applications within the pods and containers. Using authenticity protection, the communication can be protected against man-in-the-middle attacks/session hijacking and the insertion of false information into sessions.\n\nThe communication session is protected by utilizing transport encryption protocols, such as TLS. TLS provides the Kubernetes API Server with a means to be able to authenticate sessions and encrypt traffic.\n\nTo enable encrypted communication for Kubelet, the parameter client-cert-auth must be set. This parameter gives the location of the SSL Certificate Authority file used to secure Kubelet communication.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-001184"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "5376",
          "uuid": "f97c29a4-374f-5de0-b061-28ede24c9b6c",
          "stig_uuid": "92b6f33f-228f-5363-afb6-9f95dc57a4b5",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: Inherited MPN host-control recommendation for: Kubernetes etcd must enable client authentication to secure service. The official check addresses host/control-plane binaries, flags, files, native logging, node services or encryption, not an application behavior. The selected Horizon package deploys namespaced workloads atop Core and does not provision those host settings. Current scope assigns that boundary to MPN; this designation means proposed inherited coverage, not source confirmation of the exact host setting or a formal pass. No application remediation is inferred from absence of the host configuration in the application repo.\n\nComponents: MPN cluster and nodes; Gallatin horizon-uds workloads\n\nOwner: Gallatin SRE (UDS Core); MPN node/control-plane owner for host configuration\n\nNext action: Carry the exact official check into the MPN-owned Kubernetes baseline/checklist and link its inherited result; do not treat the ownership assertion as evidence of an observed native setting.\n\nEvidence:\n[host] MPN ownership\nCurrent scope assigns control plane/node OS to MPN; no host assessment or live configuration was supplied.\nhttps://gallatin.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/GG/pages/733085804/WIP+STIG+SRG+Compliance+Scope+MPN\n\n[re-kubernetes-release] re-kubernetes-release\nLatest successful Nov5 UDS push artifact2026.45.4-uds.1 identifies package commit d528b7f, Horizon b84b9af, Core1.14 and identity.mode=uds. Its build-info supplies immutable runtimeSource images; this supersedes the bundled-identity default candidate for this review.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685\n\n[re-kubernetes-supported-versions] re-kubernetes-supported-versions\nPinned Core1.14 documentation covers supported non-EOL CNCF-conformant clusters and tests1.34/1.35/1.36 variants. This supports modern-version tailoring; it does not identify the actual MPN host version.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/docs/concepts/platform/supported-distributions.mdx",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. Inherited MPN host-control recommendation for: Kubernetes etcd must enable client authentication to secure service. The official check addresses host/control-plane binaries, flags, files, native logging, node services or encryption, not an application behavior. The selected Horizon package deploys namespaced workloads atop Core and does not provision those host settings. Current scope assigns that boundary to MPN; this designation means proposed inherited coverage, not source confirmation of the exact host setting or a formal pass. No application remediation is inferred from absence of the host configuration in the application repo.\n\nNext action: Carry the exact official check into the MPN-owned Kubernetes baseline/checklist and link its inherited result; do not treat the ownership assertion as evidence of an observed native setting."
        },
        {
          "group_id_src": "V-242424",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-242424",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000219-CTR-000550",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-242424",
          "severity": "medium",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000219-CTR-000550",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-242424r1043178_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-242424r1043178",
          "rule_version": "CNTR-K8-001460",
          "rule_title": "Kubernetes Kubelet must enable tlsPrivateKeyFile for client authentication to secure service.",
          "fix_text": "On the Control Plane, run the command:\nps -ef | grep kubelet\n\nRemove the \"--tls-private-key-file\" option if present.\n\nNote the path to the config file (identified by --config).\n\nEdit the Kubernetes Kubelet config file: \nSet \"tlsPrivateKeyFile\" to  a path containing the appropriate private key. \n\nRestart the kubelet service using the following command:\nsystemctl daemon-reload && systemctl restart kubelet",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "On the Control Plane, run the command:\nps -ef | grep kubelet\n\nIf the \"--tls-private-key-file\" option exists, this is a finding. \n\nNote the path to the config file (identified by --config).\n\nRun the command:\ngrep -i tlsPrivateKeyFile <path_to_config_file>\n\nIf the setting \"tlsPrivateKeyFile\" is not set or contains no value, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Kubernetes_STIG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "Kubernetes container and pod configuration are maintained by Kubelet. Kubelet agents register nodes with the API Server, mount volume storage, and perform health checks for containers and pods. Anyone who gains access to Kubelet agents can effectively control applications within the pods and containers. Using authenticity protection, the communication can be protected against man-in-the-middle attacks/session hijacking and the insertion of false information into sessions.\n\nThe communication session is protected by utilizing transport encryption protocols such as TLS. TLS provides the Kubernetes API Server with a means to authenticate sessions and encrypt traffic.\n\nTo enable encrypted communication for Kubelet, the tlsPrivateKeyFile must be set. This parameter gives the location of the SSL Certificate Authority file used to secure Kubelet communication.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
