        {
          "group_id_src": "V-245543",
          "group_tree": [
            {
              "id": "V-245543",
              "title": "SRG-APP-000439-CTR-001080",
              "description": "<GroupDescription></GroupDescription>"
            }
          ],
          "group_id": "V-245543",
          "severity": "high",
          "group_title": "SRG-APP-000439-CTR-001080",
          "rule_id_src": "SV-245543r961632_rule",
          "rule_id": "SV-245543r961632",
          "rule_version": "CNTR-K8-002630",
          "rule_title": "Kubernetes API Server must disable token authentication to protect information in transit.",
          "fix_text": "Edit the Kubernetes API Server manifest file in the /etc/kubernetes/manifests directory on the Kubernetes Control Plane. \n\nRemove the setting \"--token-auth-file\".",
          "weight": "10.0",
          "check_content": "Change to the /etc/kubernetes/manifests/ directory on the Kubernetes Control Plane. Run the command:\ngrep -i token-auth-file * \n\nIf \"--token-auth-file\" is set in the Kubernetes API server manifest file, this is a finding.",
          "check_content_ref": {
            "href": "Kubernetes_STIG.xml",
            "name": "M"
          },
          "classification": "Unclassified",
          "discussion": "Kubernetes token authentication uses password known as secrets in a plaintext file. This file contains sensitive information such as token, username and user uid. This token is used by service accounts within pods to authenticate with the API Server. This information is very valuable for attackers with malicious intent if the service account is privileged having access to the token. With this token a threat actor can impersonate the service account gaining access to the Rest API service.",
          "false_positives": "",
          "false_negatives": "",
          "documentable": "false",
          "security_override_guidance": "",
          "potential_impacts": "",
          "third_party_tools": "",
          "ia_controls": "",
          "responsibility": "",
          "mitigations": "",
          "mitigation_control": "",
          "legacy_ids": [],
          "ccis": [
            "CCI-002448"
          ],
          "reference_identifier": "5376",
          "uuid": "11b4839b-6789-5077-9936-e0e2ea7e085d",
          "stig_uuid": "92b6f33f-228f-5363-afb6-9f95dc57a4b5",
          "status": "not_reviewed",
          "overrides": {},
          "comments": "Assessment recommendation: Likely covered\nEvidence state: source-inferred\nAssessed release: 2026.45.4-uds.1\nHorizon commit: b84b9afcd6983d553b6b8406317b6592ec90cb7c\n\nJustification: Inherited MPN host-control recommendation for: Kubernetes API Server must disable token authentication to protect information in transit. The official check addresses host/control-plane binaries, flags, files, native logging, node services or encryption, not an application behavior. The selected Horizon package deploys namespaced workloads atop Core and does not provision those host settings. Current scope assigns that boundary to MPN; this designation means proposed inherited coverage, not source confirmation of the exact host setting or a formal pass. No application remediation is inferred from absence of the host configuration in the application repo.\n\nComponents: MPN cluster and nodes; Gallatin horizon-uds workloads\n\nOwner: Gallatin SRE (UDS Core); MPN node/control-plane owner for host configuration\n\nNext action: Carry the exact official check into the MPN-owned Kubernetes baseline/checklist and link its inherited result; do not treat the ownership assertion as evidence of an observed native setting.\n\nEvidence:\n[host] MPN ownership\nCurrent scope assigns control plane/node OS to MPN; no host assessment or live configuration was supplied.\nhttps://gallatin.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/GG/pages/733085804/WIP+STIG+SRG+Compliance+Scope+MPN\n\n[re-kubernetes-release] re-kubernetes-release\nLatest successful Nov5 UDS push artifact2026.45.4-uds.1 identifies package commit d528b7f, Horizon b84b9af, Core1.14 and identity.mode=uds. Its build-info supplies immutable runtimeSource images; this supersedes the bundled-identity default candidate for this review.\nhttps://github.com/gallatinai/horizon-uds-bundle/actions/runs/42114745685\n\n[re-kubernetes-supported-versions] re-kubernetes-supported-versions\nPinned Core1.14 documentation covers supported non-EOL CNCF-conformant clusters and tests1.34/1.35/1.36 variants. This supports modern-version tailoring; it does not identify the actual MPN host version.\nhttps://github.com/defenseunicorns/uds-core/blob/c15677633cffa17e99656a7d7ccd1f98d7cb6e4d/docs/concepts/platform/supported-distributions.mdx",
          "finding_details": "Recommendation: Likely covered. Inherited MPN host-control recommendation for: Kubernetes API Server must disable token authentication to protect information in transit. The official check addresses host/control-plane binaries, flags, files, native logging, node services or encryption, not an application behavior. The selected Horizon package deploys namespaced workloads atop Core and does not provision those host settings. Current scope assigns that boundary to MPN; this designation means proposed inherited coverage, not source confirmation of the exact host setting or a formal pass. No application remediation is inferred from absence of the host configuration in the application repo.\n\nNext action: Carry the exact official check into the MPN-owned Kubernetes baseline/checklist and link its inherited result; do not treat the ownership assertion as evidence of an observed native setting."
